# Shivering Isles. A full run is a new game through the main-quest chargen and sewer cases (oblivion_main
# --to sewers_tutorial_ends --checkpoints), then this folder with `--load mwtest_sewers_tutorial_ends`.
#
# SE01Door "A Door in Niben Bay". SE01DoorScript sets 10 a game day after MQ01 90; the door's own script
# (SEDoorToShiveringIslesScript) sets it as soon as the player is within 512. Walking onto the island trips
# SE01TrigZoneREF (TrigZone01 x1.1, about 460 square round 89011 -34206): Belmyne Dreleth comes out of the door, rants
# twice (SE01BelmyneRant), Gaius Prentus says "Stay back! This one's violent!" and they fight. Belmyne's death starts the
# gate speech: four lines (SE01GateSpeech, said through the voice NPC SE01GateVoice1) count SE01Door.gatespeechVAR to
# 4, which unlocks the door. Gaius then force-greets the player (StartConversation SE01GaiusForceGreet, stage 10,
# within 512).
# DRAFT 2026-11-17 from temp/si/dial.py + temp/si/src.py: not run yet.

# The island's navmesh lies west of the trigger box (temp/si/door_island.png); the player lands there (never inside the
# box) and walks to the door, through the trigger.
case se01_island
run
cow TES4Tamriel 21 -9
wait 60
run
player.setpos x 88550
player.setpos y -34300
player.setpos z 650
wait 30
walk SE01Door1REF
until 600 GetStage SE01Door >= 10
until 900 SE01Door.BelmyneStart == 2
defend SEGaiusPrentusREF
until 3600 SEBelmyneDrelethREF.GetDead == 1
# Gaius's force-greet comes in the middle of the gate speech (run si_1a: after its 2nd line), and the speech (a
# GameMode poll) waits while that conversation is open, as Oblivion's GameMode did in a menu. So the topics come
# first: "I'd stay back from that door if I were you." (INFO 000133DC) -> "Strange Door" ("I don't know where it came
# from", 000133D8, stage 10) offers "What happened to them?" -> "I'm going in." (000133DA, goodbye) = 20.
hear 1800 SEGaiusPrentusREF stay back from that door
ask "Strange Door"
ask "What happened to them?"
ask "I'm going in."
until 300 GetStage SE01Door >= 20
bye if open
hear 1800 any Really, do come in
until 1800 SE01Door.gatespeechVAR == 4
end

# The door (SE01Door1REF) takes the player to the waiting room in the Isles. Haskill asks the player to sit
# (SE01HaskillTalk) and sits in SE01HaskillChairREF; the player takes SE01PlayerChairREF.
# Haskill's greeting "Yes. What can I do for you? I imagine you're here about the door?" (00019D69) needs him seated
# (else "Let's be civil, shall we? Please, have a seat.", a goodbye, 0005DD11: GetSitting != 3).
# The choices are gated on Haskill's own variables (GetScriptVariable): "Why did that door appear in Cyrodiil?"
# needs introWho and introWhat, "What happens now?" needs introWant and introPeople (run si_1b: after "Who are you?"
# only "What is this place?" was listed). So: "Strange Door" (000133DF) -> "Who are you?" (30, introWho) -> "What
# is this place?" (introWhat) -> "Why did that door appear in Cyrodiil?" -> "What do you want with me?" (introWant)
# -> "And the people outside?" -> "How can they be cured?" (introPeople) -> "What happens now?" -> "And if I go
# through the door?" (goodbye) = 40. Each gate's write is in the line before, so the list after it tests it.
case se01_haskill
activate SE01Door1REF
until 600 player.GetDistance SE01DoorMarkerREF < 600
wait 60
activate SE01PlayerChairREF
until 600 player.GetSitting >= 3
until 1800 SEHaskillREF.GetSitting == 3
talk SEHaskillREF
ask "Strange Door"
ask "Who are you?"
until 300 GetStage SE01Door >= 30
ask "What is this place?"
ask "Why did that door appear in Cyrodiil?"
ask "What do you want with me?"
ask "And the people outside?"
ask "How can they be cured?"
ask "What happens now?"
ask "And if I go through the door?"
until 300 GetStage SE01Door >= 40
bye if open
end

# Talking again: "Well? Have you made up your mind?" (0005E36F, say once) offers "No, thanks." / "I'll do it."; the
# second (0005E371, goodbye) sets 200, leaveVAR 1 and disables the controls. Haskill walks out
# (SE01HaskillLeavePackage; its OnPackageDone sets leaveVAR 2), the waiting room dissolves, and 23 s later
# SE01DoorScript re-enables the controls and sets 201; once the player is off the chair it sets SE02 5.
# Standing up is the player's: a moveto to the door marker stands in.
case se01_join
talk SEHaskillREF
ask "I'll do it."
until 300 GetStage SE01Door >= 200
until 1800 SEHaskillREF.leaveVAR == 2
until 3600 GetStage SE01Door >= 201
run
player.moveto SE01DoorMarkerREF
until 900 GetStage SE02 >= 5
end
